# Nothing installed, built or secret is ever copied into an image.
#
# The image this app used to build had no ignore file and a `COPY . .` after
# `npm ci`, so the 352 MB node_modules directory sitting in the working copy
# was copied over the freshly installed one — the build shipped whatever
# happened to be on the machine.
#
# Note on precedence: the Dockerfile now builds from the repository root, so
# the file Docker consults is the root /.dockerignore, which excludes the same
# paths for every app. This one still matters for a directory-scoped build
# (`docker build agro-sentinel/web`, which is what a developer types first)
# and it documents the intent where the Dockerfile is.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
*.local
